edby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T20:00:13-07:00","id":1419502,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Classic Universal of the 30s (and part of the 40s and 50s). Italian Giallo. <br /> <br /> I'd suggest classic British horror, but I suspect that the main game will already be delving into that quite a bit. Maybe Mexican horror films. Or J-Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T16:44:01-07:00","id":1419673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1415954-beyond-the-grave-they-came-from-camp-murder-lake?p=1419502#post1419502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Classic Universal of the 30s (and part of the 40s and 50s). Italian Giallo.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest classic British horror, but I suspect that the main game will already be delving into that quite a bit. Maybe Mexican horror films. Or J-Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>J-Horror would be good. Its very different from western horror and would lend itself to a film horror type game. I haven't seen to much mexican horror, maybe some badly dubbed vampire films from the 60s so I can't really comment on those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T23:03:53-07:00","id":1419723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1415954-beyond-the-grave-they-came-from-camp-murder-lake?p=1419673#post1419673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">J-Horror would be good. Its very different from western horror and would lend itself to a film horror type game. I haven't seen to much mexican horror, maybe some badly dubbed vampire films from the 60s so I can't really comment on those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I would personally help finance a Beyond the Grave sourcebook about Mexico and Mexican horror just to have rules for masked wrestlers fighting monsters, because I am that kind of dork.<br /> <br /> El Santo vs. Blackula would be awesome. Search your feelings; You know it to be true.<br /> <br /> <br /> (It does occur to me that some sort of Beyond the Grave Companion or World Guide that looked at 60s and 70s horror trends/genres/film cultures around the globe and how to do them in BtG would be really cool. Chapters for the Italy, Mexico, the UK, Japan, Hong Kong/Taiwan, and so forth. Maybe also some of the regional differences for places like New England, New Orleans, Toronto and the like. And perhaps a look at some of the specifics of Blaxsploitation horror.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-23-2020, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:55:04-07:00","id":1419773,"title":"","content":"There is the NWE! book coming out for Trinity Continuum which might scratch that itch for you, No One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T20:38:17-07:00","id":1420210,"title":"","content":"I mention a World Guide type thing for Beyond the Grave, but it also occurs to me that such a thing would also be pretty interesting/useful for Beneath the Sea as well. The 1950s aquatic monster genre in Japan, for example, would be kind of ea